WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.538 --> 00:00:01.504
(cheerful music)

00:00:01.504 --> 00:00:02.754
- [Voiceover] Settlers of Catan

00:00:02.754 --> 00:00:05.441
is one of the best-selling
board games of all time.

00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.945
And nestled in the rolling
hills of Rossdorf, Germany,

00:00:09.945 --> 00:00:12.047
on this picturesque street,

00:00:12.047 --> 00:00:14.277
past the buzzer in building 43,

00:00:14.277 --> 00:00:16.718
and standing in the back of the garden

00:00:16.718 --> 00:00:20.718
is Klaus Teuber, the man
who made it all happen.

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:28.095
Settlers of Catan is a board
game for up to four players

00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:31.881
where you collect resources to
build settlements and cities.

00:00:31.881 --> 00:00:33.354
They're worth points.

00:00:33.354 --> 00:00:35.381
First to ten wins.

00:00:35.381 --> 00:00:36.978
(triumphant music)

00:00:36.978 --> 00:00:39.116
And it all started like this.

00:00:39.116 --> 00:00:43.283
- In the '90s and '80s, I
lead a dental laboratory.

00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:49.244
Developing games was a
little bit a refuge for me.

00:00:49.244 --> 00:00:51.486
- [Voiceover] His first
game was called Barbarossa.

00:00:51.486 --> 00:00:55.543
- When I made Barbarossa,
I was in my early 30s.

00:00:55.543 --> 00:00:59.710
I feel that this is a kind
of thing I like very much,

00:01:00.574 --> 00:01:03.927
developing games, and it
could be in the future for me

00:01:03.927 --> 00:01:06.391
a very, very good hobby.

00:01:06.391 --> 00:01:08.465
- [Voiceover] He designed
a handful of other games,

00:01:08.465 --> 00:01:10.863
and then made Catan.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:13.555
(cheerful music)

00:01:13.555 --> 00:01:16.526
Klaus had become
interested in Viking tales.

00:01:16.526 --> 00:01:19.781
- Yes, and the story of
the Vikings inspired me.

00:01:19.781 --> 00:01:22.740
I imagined how they reach Iceland.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.209
They need wood, they need
houses and other things,

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:29.376
and so, out of this
imagination I developed Catan.

00:01:32.127 --> 00:01:36.063
- [Voiceover] From design to
market, it was a family affair.

00:01:36.063 --> 00:01:37.805
This is Benny Teuber.

00:01:37.805 --> 00:01:41.737
He lives in Germany, and
he is Klaus's youngest son.

00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:44.312
And this is Guido Teuber.

00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:46.047
(clears throat)

00:01:46.047 --> 00:01:47.672
And this is Guido Teuber.

00:01:47.672 --> 00:01:49.639
He lives in San Francisco.

00:01:49.639 --> 00:01:51.741
He is Klaus's eldest son.

00:01:51.741 --> 00:01:54.727
- In my family, I am
one of the game testers,

00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:56.214
along with my mom.

00:01:56.214 --> 00:01:57.047
- Me, too.

00:01:58.552 --> 00:02:02.424
We playtested the Settlers
of Catan quite often.

00:02:02.424 --> 00:02:05.388
- We would all get together
at the dining room table

00:02:05.388 --> 00:02:08.785
and would test and assess games.

00:02:08.785 --> 00:02:10.732
- Sometimes he put a Mickey Mouse comic

00:02:10.732 --> 00:02:13.077
next to my chair, so in
case the game was boring,

00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:16.419
he knew that I would read it
instead of playing the game.

00:02:16.419 --> 00:02:20.085
- My dad took that and
tweaked it, worked on it.

00:02:20.085 --> 00:02:23.770
So this was sort of an
exciting moment for my dad.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.080
- [Voiceover] In the Teuber family,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.449
there's a bit of competition.

00:02:26.449 --> 00:02:29.029
- My father would probably
say I'm the best player.

00:02:29.029 --> 00:02:30.598
- No.

00:02:30.598 --> 00:02:33.283
- Sorry, Dad, Benny is the best.

00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:34.116
- Hmm.

00:02:35.787 --> 00:02:37.242
- [Guido] There is a bit of a rivalry

00:02:37.242 --> 00:02:38.425
between my dad and my brother.

00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:39.598
(cards falling)

00:02:39.598 --> 00:02:41.132
(laughing)

00:02:41.132 --> 00:02:43.530
(light music)

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.886
- [Voiceover] Catan was
officially released in Germany

00:02:45.886 --> 00:02:49.354
in 1994, and it was an immediate success.

00:02:49.354 --> 00:02:51.944
- We had immediate success in Germany,

00:02:51.944 --> 00:02:54.457
because we won Game of the Year.

00:02:54.457 --> 00:02:55.878
- [Voiceover] Worldwide to date,

00:02:55.878 --> 00:02:58.948
over 24 million copies have been sold.

00:02:58.948 --> 00:03:01.252
- This game was born out of a story,

00:03:01.252 --> 00:03:03.542
but it also creates stories.

00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:05.270
- The beauty of Catan is that in the end,

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.192
you still have constructed something.

00:03:07.192 --> 00:03:09.671
So, in a way, everybody wins.

00:03:09.671 --> 00:03:13.732
- It was my wish to have
a very peaceful game,

00:03:13.732 --> 00:03:17.402
with a lot of interaction
bringing people together.

00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:19.735
For me, Catan was a success.

00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:25.449
- [Voiceover] To all the
Catan fans out there,

00:03:25.449 --> 00:03:27.160
here's some advice.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.646
- Well, you always have
to follow your strategy,

00:03:29.646 --> 00:03:31.356
but also you have to complain quite a bit,

00:03:31.356 --> 00:03:32.828
even though you know you're winning,

00:03:32.828 --> 00:03:34.286
you still have to say you're not.

00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:37.294
- I love building cities as
early as possible in the game.

00:03:37.294 --> 00:03:41.291
- Never build the longest
road at the beginning.

00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:43.001
- [Voiceover] And there you have it.

00:03:43.001 --> 00:03:45.584
(guitar music)

